                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "@echasnovski just wanted to inform you about my findings since the initial issue was regarding navigating back to the git diff buffer. I used ``tabe`` instead of ``vertical split`` in your given example and I could navigate back to the diff source by closing the buffer opened with ``tabe``. I just wanted to ask if this functionality can be included in mini-git with a different option as part of ``MiniGit.show_diff_source({opts})`` or to that matter as a different function.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a> just wanted to inform you about my findings since the initial issue was regarding navigating back to the git diff buffer. I used <code class=\"notranslate\">tabe</code> instead of <code class=\"notranslate\">vertical split</code> in your given example and I could navigate back to the diff source by closing the buffer opened with <code class=\"notranslate\">tabe</code>. I just wanted to ask if this functionality can be included in mini-git with a different option as part of <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniGit.show_diff_source({opts})</code> or to that matter as a different function.</p>",
