                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "`MiniGit.show_diff_source` [does support showing in separate tab](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f0d6e89515c6b055c20d257da717bd30211532f1/doc/mini-git.txt#L304-L305). It would still be not the file from disk, but special 'mini.git' buffer with the same content and possibly highlighting. No other approach in showing 'mini.git' output (be it `show_at_cursor()`, `:Git`, `show_diff_source()`, and others) apart from already implemented is not planned.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniGit.show_diff_source</code> <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f0d6e89515c6b055c20d257da717bd30211532f1/doc/mini-git.txt#L304-L305\">does support showing in separate tab</a>. It would still be not the file from disk, but special 'mini.git' buffer with the same content and possibly highlighting. No other approach in showing 'mini.git' output (be it <code class=\"notranslate\">show_at_cursor()</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">:Git</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">show_diff_source()</code>, and others) apart from already implemented is not planned.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "MiniGit.show_diff_source does support showing in separate tab. It would still be not the file from disk, but special 'mini.git' buffer with the same content and possibly highlighting. No other approach in showing 'mini.git' output (be it show_at_cursor(), :Git, show_diff_source(), and others) apart from already implemented is not planned.",
